n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={g}^{′}(x)+{h}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288323 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288324 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1041 "field-1" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288323 13194139534440 true] [17592186288322 1110 #uuid "08870b2c-471f-5033-a2ba-4e7dc4788a0b" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288323 1034 "\\sec(2x)\\tan(2x)-x^3" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534440 true] [17592186288323 1111 #uuid "3c7087fd-7c30-5281-a0ee-5234d0a417c3" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288324 1034 "\\sec(2x)\\tan(2x)+x^3" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534440 true] [17592186288324 1111 #uuid "238c9da1-0e86-5356-821c-3077ad7a39d6" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288326 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288328 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288330 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1089 "q-342443" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1100 "Given that $y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)),$ we have\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sec}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)\\operatorname{tan}⁡($\n{{field-3}} $).$" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1113 #uuid "da7a9363-596e-552e-8139-fc1c28e7c1ea" 13194139534440 true] [17592186288325 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u),\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, a